# vsce does not read .gitignore: without this file, the .vsix would carry
# src/, test/, tsconfig.json and above all .superpowers/ (internal review
# reports, private paths). Explicit allowlist: everything is excluded by
# default, and only what the extension needs at runtime is brought back in.
#
# Every re-included entry must stay a pattern ending in a wildcard segment
# (e.g. `out/**`) or an exact file (e.g. `bin/koh-vibe-bridge`), never a bare
# folder name (`!scripts`): vsce automatically expands that to `scripts/**`
# and then brings the whole folder back in, not just the targeted file —
# which would have pulled bump-version.sh and capture-fixtures.sh into the
# package.
**

!out/**
!resources/**
!bin/koh-vibe-bridge
!bin/koh-vibe-statusline
!scripts/install-hooks.cjs
!build-info.json
!l10n/**
!package.nls.json
!package.nls.fr.json
!package.json
!LICENSE
!README.md
!README.fr.md
!CHANGELOG.md
